{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's motion and perception interface, with open-loop motion pulses and sensor events. The specification enforces safe, coverage-oriented exploration: random_walk is preferred in clear states, move_forward is used for short progress, and recovery turns are used after obstacles. Recovery is conservative but not excessive; full_rotate is reserved for rare, persistent blockages. All obstacle events force a turn recovery before returning to exploration. The design ensures no state enables both rotate directions, and random_walk is never enabled in obstacle states.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for motion-perception interface and for exploration policy.",
    "Specification ensures: (1) random_walk is used in clear/search states, (2) move_forward is used for short progress, (3) rotate_clockwise/rotate_counterclockwise are used for recovery, (4) full_rotate is only used after repeated blockages, (5) all obstacle events force a turn recovery, (6) no oscillations or infinite controllable loops."
  ],
